modules.docstring:
Bounded foreground activation for an already validated task window.

UIA SetFocus only focuses an element. Activation uses Win32 window APIs;
no synthetic Alt keys, shell commands, privilege changes or global clicks.

Automatic metrics for the ablation experiment (plan sections 10-20).

Everything here is deterministic rule-based diagnostics over replayed
replies. Per plan section 12 they are AGGREGATE diagnostics only — never
a single-reply verdict — and per Phase 13 Tier 3 the human blind
evaluation is the final judge. Every detection rule is transparent and
bilingual (CN/EN); weights live in plain constants below.

Machine-only surfaces computed here:

- per-reply flags + lengths + 4gram self-overlap vs prior history;
- case-aware rates (unprompted question / advice only when the case
  forbids them, plan section 11);
- assistant_template_score 0-8 (plan section 13);
- dialogue closure pressure (plan section 14);
- length distribution incl. coefficient of variation (plan section 15);
- cross-character style distance without embeddings (plan section 16);
- Anti-Assistantness machine sub-score /20 (Phase 16, penalty-oriented,
  case-aware so warm_poetic's legitimate care is not punished as AI);
- Knowledge/Memory structural safety (resolved answer byte-identical
  across conditions — verified against fixtures, plan section 22/F5).

NOT computed here: LLM-judge and human scores (Tier 2/3), Tapestry
composite (report.py merges those when score files exist).

OpenAI Chat Completions route client tests (ADR 0014, batch 2).

All HTTP goes through monkeypatched ``transport`` helpers — no test ever
touches a real endpoint (plan §17).  Covers plan §16 group C:
- payload shape (model verbatim, messages, stream flags, tools);
- sampling merge order and None/unknown-key filtering;
- MiniMax-profile think stripping (streaming + buffered, split chunks);
- snapshot freezing (later mutation of source dicts does not leak);
- key never appears in the debug description view.

Provider registry storage tests (ADR 0014, batch 1).

Covers plan §16 groups A and D at the storage layer:
- absent registry == inherit (legacy configuration untouched);
- repeatable table creation, legacy tables readable;
- binding save/reset semantics (reset never writes a concrete model);
- delete guards for referenced models/accounts;
- credential references never leak plaintext through getters;
- failed saves keep the previous binding;
- base URL security validation.

symbols.docstring:
Discard one role's workers if the singleton already exists.

This helper is deliberately no-op when the pet policy was never used;
role deletion must not instantiate a background worker as a side effect.

